# openldap FHS migration: slapd runtime /run/slapd -> /var/run/slapd.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - pidfile/argsfile: overwritten by slapd at every start; stale
#   files are never validated or deleted.
# - ldapi socket: upstream default derives from --localstatedir
#   (/var/run/slapd/slapd.sock); recreated by the daemon on start.
# - New /var/run/slapd: converged here on upgrade (ldap:ldap 0755);
#   created by checkpath (OpenRC) and the unit drop-in (systemd).
# - Old /run/slapd: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once empty;
#   left in place and reported while the old server runs.
# - NOTED, untouched: the upstream systemd unit runs slapd without
#   -u/-g (root) while slapd.initd drops to ldap:ldap. Identity
#   alignment is an author decision, not part of this path move.

dir /var/run/slapd 0755 ldap ldap
rmdir-if-empty /run/slapd
